Java generator 0.5.2 has a reproduced native error-buffer cleanup alias bug.
This project applies the local MPL-2.0 correction
lox-archive-java-0.5.2-rustbuffer-free-owned-status-2, specified in
patches/uniffi-bindgen-java-0.5.2-rustbuffer-free.json, after generation.
It copies a RustBuffer descriptor before nested cleanup resets reusable
call status. It also gives each ClockClient owned wait dispatch a confined
call-status arena closed before the dispatch returns, including exceptional exit. Other
caller threads use GC-managed automatic arenas: reclamation there is eventual,
not deterministic before GC. Nested owned scopes restore the outer status;
the slab allocator for returned FFM views is unchanged.
Generator version, complete input/output SHA256s for BOTH changed helpers,
and exact reviewed fragment counts are mandatory; mismatches stop builds.
The source jar contains the corrected helper, and both JVM jars carry the
patch specification and application receipt in META-INF/lox-build.
Do not substitute unpatched generator output. Native ABI checks remain on.
Only RustBuffer.java and UniffiHelpers.java are changed. These MPL notices do not claim
ownership of upstream code or relicense this repository's own source.

The project-authored lox_archive_async.py and Java ClockClient /
ClockDispatchTimeout sources retain the project license. These stdlib-only
adapters bound host offload of generated native waits and explicitly forward
cancel/shutdown to the same production Rust driver. They do not implement
HTTP, protocol decoding, retries or validation. Java sources are included in
the sources jar; the Python adapter is included in the wheel.

maturin 1.16.0 is a build-only tool (MIT OR Apache-2.0), not a runtime Python
dependency. JDK/Kotlin compilers are external tools, not bundled in the API
jar. The Kotlin test jar includes its own standard library for testing only;
it is not the distributed native API jar.

Other transitive Rust libraries retain their own licenses. Cargo.lock pins
their versions/checksums; maturin's wheel SBOM records the dependency graph.
This focused notice is not a replacement for their source/license notices.
